  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Bohr suggest a formulae to calculate the radius and energy of each orbit and gave the following formulae<br /><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />Where except <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> , all other unit are constant so <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∝</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> .",
